      "problem": "$\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-5{sec}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C, \\\\ \\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-5{sec}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x-\\int 5{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x-5\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-5\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
